-- allium: 3
--
-- nixtune: a declarative network music player. A NixOS module
-- (services.nixtune.*) plus a PureScript (Halogen) page, built as a
-- public flake and consumed by the neoblade-config fleet as one input
-- and one row. A clean reimplementation of what moOde audio player
-- does, with none of moOde's code, none of its name, and none of its
-- runtime configuration machinery.
--
-- STATE OF THE WORLD, 2026-10-30, 19:30. The hardware works, the room
-- page works, and the ambition has grown: this revision records what
-- shipped since 03:00, specifies the next page (one transport bar and a
-- three-column tag browser), and names the point at which the DJ
-- ambition stops being an extension of this design and becomes a
-- different one.
--
--   Repositories:
--     ~/git/nixtune             the public flake, PUSHED to
--                               github:harryprayiv/nixtune. nix/module/
--                               {default,hardware,mpd,library,database,
--                               volume,art,ui,airplay,upnp}.nix,
--                               packages/upmpdcli.nix,
--                               packages/nixtune-web/. Its flake.lock
--                               pins nixpkgs to 6510408d (KnownIssue
--                               purescript_segfault). A devShell carries
--                               spago from purescript-overlay for editing
--                               the lock; consumers never evaluate it.
--     ~/neoblade-config         the fleet. Input `nixtune` =
--                               github:harryprayiv/nixtune, nixpkgs
--                               following. The input is a GITHUB input,
--                               so a change in the working tree is
--                               invisible to the fleet until it is
--                               pushed and `nix flake update nixtune
--                               --tarball-ttl 0` has run. A night was
--                               lost to that once. Adapter role
--                               modules/system/player.nix; rows `nixtune`
--                               (aarch64, Pi) and `nixtune-vm` (x86 QEMU);
--                               facts in hosts/nixtune.nix and
--                               hosts/nixtune-vm.nix. deployAddr is the
--                               NAME nixtune.lan, which the router's DNS
--                               gives to whichever interface holds the
--                               lease.
--
--   The library, measured 2026-10-30: about 55k MP3 and 18.5k FLAC
--   entries in MPD's tag_cache. Roughly a quarter lossless. No cover
--   files beside the audio anywhere; the art is inside the files, as
--   ID3v2 APIC frames and FLAC PICTURE blocks. Every album directory
--   also carries Synology's @eaDir and .checksums, which are pruned
--   everywhere the player walks the tree. A queue of 220 entries is an
--   ordinary working size, which is the load the page is measured at.
--
--   Verified on the Pi (Raspberry Pi 5 Model B Rev 1.1, HiFiBerry DAC2
--   HD, Samsung 128 GB card):
--     - Boots the generic aarch64 SD image with U-Boot chainloaded by the
--       GPU firmware.
--     - The DAC appears as ALSA card sndrpihifiberry with mixer control
--       DAC, limits 0 to 240 in 0.5 dB steps.
--     - mpd, nixtune-websocket, nginx, shairport-sync, nixtune-volume
--       and its websocat bridge all active.
--     - /srv/music mounts from the Synology; the rescan timer runs two
--       minutes after boot and daily.
--     - Wifi: secrets/nixtune.yaml holds user-password and wifi-psk.
--
--   Lessons that cost a night, written down so they are not paid twice:
--     - nixpkgs' online first-boot resize of the ext4 root corrupted
--       directory blocks across the store; grow the card OFFLINE on
--       winsmuth. KnownIssue sd_resize.
--     - MPD's auto_update installs inotify watches over the whole tree
--       on its main thread before notifying systemd; on a vast NFS
--       library this exceeded the start timeout, and inotify never fires
--       for NFS writes anyway. Off; a timer runs `mpc update`.
--     - websocat -t frames by TCP READ, not by line. One websocket
--       message can hold a whole MPD reply or stop in the middle of a
--       line. The page accumulates a partial tail and splits on newline.
--       Before that fix the page had never read a single reply from the
--       real player, and three rounds of blaming browser caching went by
--       first.
--     - Every file in the Nix store has mtime 1970-01-01. nginx sends
--       that as Last-Modified with no lifetime and a browser applies
--       heuristic freshness, about five years. The page is served
--       no-store with etag and if_modified_since off.
--     - MPD URIs are relative to music_directory. Changing the export
--       silently invalidates every URI in the database and the queue
--       fails without saying why. database.nix stamps the export beside
--       the database and drops the database on a mismatch.
--     - MPD closes a client whose reply overruns its output buffer.
--       `listall` on this library does it; so does an unwindowed
--       `search any` on a common word. Every unbounded listing command
--       is either windowed or not used. KnownIssue listall_overruns.
--     - Halogen writes an input's value property on every render, which
--       clears the browser's dirty flag, so a controlled input never
--       fires `change`. A typed value is committed on Enter and on blur.
--     - e2fsprogs and parted are not on winsmuth; every tool outside
--       coreutils and util-linux is invoked through `nix shell`.
--
-- Design decisions that shape this spec:
--
--   1. The only source of configuration is the Nix declaration. No
--      settings database, no settings page, no daemon that rewrites
--      /etc or /boot. Decision 21 is where this is under pressure.
--   2. Every optional capability is a sub-option with an enable flag
--      defaulting to false; a disabled one contributes nothing.
--   3. The page is a Halogen single page application that speaks the
--      MPD protocol itself over websockets bridged by websocat. There is
--      no application server on the Pi. Decisions 8, 14 and 15 are all
--      consequences of holding this line, and decision 22 is where it
--      would have to break.
--   4. No over the air updates. Updates arrive only as new generations.
--   5. The root filesystem is NOT ephemeral yet; the module publishes
--      persistPaths and the fleet adapter maps it into the manifest.
--      persistPaths is no longer readOnly: more than one part of the
--      module owns state, and the definitions merge.
--   6. Two layers, one boundary: the public module knows no fleet; the
--      adapter maps fleet facts into its options.
--   7. Maintenance is `nix flake update` on an update branch, CI, merge.
--
-- Decisions taken 2026-10-30 (the page as a room's player):
--   8. ROLES WITHOUT A BACKEND. Two pages from one bundle: the guest
--      page at / and the host page at /host. The QR code on the host
--      page encodes the guest URL. There is no token and no rotation.
--      THE CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly: role limits are enforced by the
--      page, not by the Pi. Both pages reach the same websocket, and a
--      guest who opens a browser console can send any MPD command. This
--      is accepted for a LAN of invited people. A filtering proxy
--      between websocat and MPD is the upgrade path.
--   9. GUESTS APPEND ONLY. A guest sees now playing (read-only) and the
--      library, and may add a track or a folder to the END of the queue.
--      Guests do not see the queue, do not remove or reorder, do not
--      skip, do not touch transport or volume.
--  10. GUEST IDENTITY IS A NICKNAME PER DEVICE, generated by the page on
--      first visit (adjective plus animal), kept in that browser's
--      localStorage, never prompted for. Attribution lives in MPD
--      stickers under nixtune.added_by.
--  11. LIBRARY = Music/ ONLY. library.export points at
--      /volume2/music/Music. The first scan runs for days in the
--      background; the page shows a quiet indicator until updating_db
--      clears, and everything already scanned is browsable meanwhile.
--      database.nix disables all nine playlist plugins so only audio is
--      indexed.
--  13. THE QR IS BUILT BY NIX: qrencode renders the guest URL to qr.svg
--      in the closure. No QR library in the bundle.
--
-- Decisions taken 2026-10-30 evening, from running the thing:
--
--  12. SUPERSEDED. "No cover art" lasted one day. See decision 15.
--
--  14. THE HARDWARE VOLUME IS WRITTEN BY A HELPER, NOT BY MPD.
--      MPD sets volume through snd_mixer_selem_set_playback_dB_all
--      (src/mixer/plugins/VolumeMapping.cxx) whenever the control's dB
--      range exceeds 24 dB. The DAC2 HD's range is 120 dB, so MPD always
--      takes that path, and on this card every setvol through it lands
--      on raw 0, a hard mute that stays. Measured: five consecutive
--      setvol commands at 30, 60, 90, 40 and 75 all left the control at
--      0. The same card takes amixer writes, raw and mapped, and they
--      hold.
--      So: MPD keeps the mixer for READING, which is how the page and
--      every other client learn the level and how AirPlay changes show
--      up. WRITES go to a systemd socket-activated shell helper running
--      `amixer -M`, reached from the browser through websocat and nginx
--      at /volume. This is the split moOde uses (www/util/vol.sh calls
--      `amixer -M -c $CARDNUM sset "$AMIXNAME" $LEVEL%`), without
--      moOde's database or PHP.
--      The scale is ALSA's normalized mapping, percent = 10^(dB/60),
--      which is what both amixer -M and MPD report, so the number the
--      page sends and the number MPD sends back mean the same thing.
--      This is already perceptual: a level that looks linear on the bar
--      is logarithmic in power, which is the behaviour wanted.
--      capabilities.volumePath is the path or null; null means the host
--      has no such card and MPD's own setvol is used.
--
--  15. COVER ART IS A CACHE THE PLAYER BUILDS. This library keeps its
--      art inside the files and nothing in the serving path can read
--      that: nginx serves files, and MPD's albumart and readpicture
--      answer with binary that a text-mode websocket cannot carry.
--      art.nix walks the library on a timer, takes a picture file beside
--      the audio when there is one and otherwise pulls the embedded
--      picture out of the first track with ffmpeg, and writes exactly
--      one cover.jpg per album directory under /var/lib/nixtune/art,
--      mirroring the library's layout. nginx serves that tree and only
--      that tree, so /art/ can never reach audio. The page asks for one
--      URL per album and gets one 404 at worst.
--      The unit is niced to 19 with idle IO and idle CPU scheduling. The
--      first pass over tens of thousands of tracks runs for a long while
--      and must not disturb playback. Afterwards only album directories
--      whose mtime moved cost anything, so art added later appears
--      without clearing the cache by hand.
--
--  16. THE PAGE IS SEVERAL MODULES, NOT ONE. Main.purs reached 1278
--      lines and became impossible to hand over in one piece. It is now
--      Types, Net, Volume, Reorder, Art, Nick, Page, Ui and Main, none
--      over about 300 lines. This is a delivery constraint made into a
--      structural one, and the structure is better for it: Types knows
--      nothing, Page draws and performs no effects, Main is the state
--      machine and the protocol.
--
--  17. ONE ATTRIBUTION QUERY, NOT ONE PER ENTRY. The first version asked
--      `sticker get song <uri> nixtune.added_by` for every queue entry
--      and never recorded a miss, so a queue of 220 cost 220 round trips
--      on every queue change, forever. `sticker find song "" <name>`
--      returns every attribution in one command. The page subscribes to
--      MPD's `sticker` idle subsystem to stay current. At 220 entries
--      this is the difference between a page that answers a drag and one
--      that appears broken.
--
--  18. ONE TRANSPORT BAR. NEW, not yet built. Today the transport sits
--      on the Now playing view and the volume sits in a bar pinned to
--      the bottom of every view. That means browsing the library with
--      music playing offers no way to skip a track. Transport and volume
--      become ONE bottom frame, present on every host view: previous,
--      play/pause, next, then the level. The bar is the player; the
--      views above it are the library, the queue and what is on now.
--      Crowding is the risk and the answer is a budget, not a
--      compromise: at phone width the bar shows previous, play/pause,
--      next, mute and the slider, and the typed level field and the
--      steppers appear only at 30rem and up. Nothing is removed at any
--      width; the two controls that have keyboard and gesture
--      equivalents are the ones that fold away.
--
--  19. BROWSE BY TAG, NOT ONLY BY FOLDER. NEW, not yet built. A
--      directory tree is the wrong shape for choosing music in a room.
--      The Library view gains a three-column browser over MPD's tag
--      database: genre, then artist, then album, each column filtered by
--      the selection to its left, with the track list below or beside
--      the third column. The folder tree stays as a fourth way in, not
--      as the default.
--      The protocol is `list genre`, `list artist genre "<g>"`,
--      `list album artist "<a>"` and `find album "<x>" artist "<a>"`.
--      Every one of those is bounded by the selection above it, so none
--      of them can overrun MPD's output buffer the way `listall` does,
--      with one exception: `list artist` with no filter over this
--      library is large and is windowed.
--      A LETTER RAIL runs down the side of any column over about fifty
--      entries: A to Z plus #, tapping one scrolls that column to the
--      first entry under that letter. It is page-side arithmetic over a
--      list the page already holds, so it costs no request and no
--      backend. This is the thing most missed while scrolling a library
--      this size.
--
--  20. HOME ASSISTANT TALKS TO MPD DIRECTLY. It ships an MPD
--      integration that speaks the same protocol nixtune's page speaks.
--      Nothing is added to the module: services.nixtune.mpd.exposeOnLan
--      = true opens 6600 on the LAN and HA connects to nixtune.lan:6600.
--      It can then play, pause, skip, set volume and load playlists, and
--      can be triggered by anything HA can trigger on.
--      Two things follow from decision 14. HA's volume control calls
--      setvol, which on this card mutes it. Until that is handled, HA
--      should be used for transport and not for volume, and the handling
--      is an open question below. HA is also an unauthenticated client
--      on the LAN with full MPD rights, which is the same trust model as
--      decision 8 and is accepted on the same grounds.
--
--  21. DSP IS A CONFIG-TIME CHOICE. MPD's filter plugins are declared in
--      mpd.conf, so a parametric EQ or a room correction curve is a
--      services.nixtune.dsp.* option and a rebuild to change it. That is
--      slower than a slider and it is the honest consequence of decision
--      1. The alternative, a daemon that rewrites mpd.conf and restarts
--      MPD, is the beginning of moOde's settings database and is
--      refused. A middle path exists and is not yet chosen: ALSA plugins
--      (ladspa, camilladsp) read their own coefficient files, which
--      could live in a persisted path that a page writes, leaving the
--      declaration to say THAT there is DSP and the file to say what it
--      does. That still needs something on the Pi that can write a file
--      on request, which is decision 22's problem.
--
--  22. THE DJ AMBITION FORKS HERE, AND THE FORK IS NAMED NOW. The stated
--      goal is a party DJ device: crossfade, DSP, beat matching. These
--      are three different distances from what exists.
--        CROSSFADE is free. `crossfade <seconds>` and `mixrampdb` are
--        MPD protocol commands. A control on the transport bar and a
--        default in the declaration, nothing more. In scope.
--        DSP is decision 21: an option and a rebuild, or a coefficient
--        file and a writer. Partly in scope.
--        BEAT MATCHING IS NOT AN EXTENSION OF THIS DESIGN. It needs two
--        decks sounding at once, independent tempo and pitch on each, a
--        cue point and preview path, and a crossfader. MPD is one deck
--        and one queue; its crossfade overlaps the tail of one track
--        with the head of the next and that is the whole of it. There is
--        no MPD protocol command that will ever do this.
--        A DJ console therefore means a second audio path beside MPD, an
--        audio engine on the Pi, and an application server to drive it,
--        which contradicts decision 3. The spec records this as a
--        SEPARATE PRODUCT sharing the library, the hardware profile and
--        the fleet row, not as a later release of this one. Calling it
--        nixtune's next version would quietly delete the property that
--        makes nixtune worth having, which is that the whole player is
--        one declaration and nothing on the box holds state.
--        What IS in scope, and worth doing first because it covers most
--        of a party: crossfade, consume as the default queue discipline,
--        a queue that is pleasant to reorder under load, replay gain,
--        and the tag browser that makes finding the next record fast.
--
-- Earlier decisions still in force: AirPlay on, UPnP off until upmpdcli
-- builds, SD card on oracle's boot path, hardware profile from the
-- datasheet.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Given
------------------------------------------------------------

given {
    host: HostDeclaration
    player: Player
    output: OutputDevice
    module_repo: ProjectRepository
    fleet_repo: FleetConfig
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

external entity FleetConfig {
    repo_path: String
    input_url: String
    adapter_module: String
    build_command: String
}

-- A browser on the LAN. Identity is a nickname the page made up and
-- stored in that browser; nothing on the Pi knows who anyone is.
external entity Client {
    address: String
    on_lan: Boolean
    nickname: String?
}

external entity Nas {
    address: String
    export: String
    allows: Set<String>
}

-- Anything on the LAN speaking the MPD protocol to port 6600 directly:
-- Home Assistant, mpc, a phone client. Not a session; it has no page
-- and no nickname, and the player cannot tell it from any other client.
external entity ProtocolClient {
    kind: home_assistant | mpc | other
    address: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

value SystemClosure {
    store_path: String
    flake_revision: String
}

value Track {
    uri: String
    title: String?
    artist: String?
    album: String?
    genre: String?
    duration: Duration?
    format: AudioFormat?
}

-- What a file is, from its container. MPD's own audio figures describe
-- what the decoder hands the DAC, which is a different question.
value AudioFormat {
    label: String
    quality: lossless | lossy
}

-- What nix/module/ui.nix writes to capabilities.json at build time.
value Capabilities {
    hostname: String
    profile: String
    output_kind: alsa | null_output
    card: String?
    mixer: String?
    modules: Set<ModuleKind>
    library: Boolean
    stations: List<RadioStation>
    websocket_path: String
    volume_path: String?
    art_path: String?
    max_volume: Integer
    public_url: String
    host_path: String
}

-- One column of the tag browser and the state of its selection.
value BrowseColumn {
    axis: BrowseAxis
    entries: List<String>
    selected: String?
    windowed: Boolean
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

contract PlayerModule {
    evaluate: (declaration: HostDeclaration) -> SystemClosure

    @invariant Purity
        -- Evaluation reads only the Nix declaration and pinned inputs.

    @invariant Determinism
        -- Same declaration, same lock, same closure.

    @invariant LazyModules
        -- A disabled sub-option contributes nothing to the closure.

    @invariant NoRuntimeConfiguration
        -- Nothing in the closure writes to /etc, /boot or the store at
        -- runtime. The art cache under /var/lib/nixtune is derived data,
        -- rebuildable from the library at any time, and is declared in
        -- persistPaths only because rebuilding it is expensive.

    @invariant FleetAgnostic
        -- The module references only nixpkgs' option tree, its own
        -- services.nixtune.*, and, when present, nixos-hardware's
        -- hardware.raspberry-pi.* (guarded).

    @guidance
        -- Options as implemented:
        --   enable
        --   hardware.profile            "pi5-dac2hd" | "none"
        --   library.export              "host:/path" or null
        --   wifi.ssid, wifi.pskFile
        --   mpd.port, mpd.exposeOnLan, mpd.maxVolume
        --   mpd.consume                 null to remember, true/false to
        --                               set at every MPD start
        --   radio.stations
        --   ui.enable, ui.package, ui.port
        --   ui.publicUrl, ui.hostPath
        --   ui.albumArt, ui.albumArtSize
        --   arbitration.resumeAfterRenderer
        --   renderers.airplay.{enable,name}
        --   renderers.upnp.{enable,friendlyName,package}
        --   persistPaths (merged), output.* (internal)
        --   volume.path (internal, set by volume.nix)
        --   art.path (internal, set by art.nix)
        -- Options this revision adds:
        --   mpd.crossfade               Integer seconds, 0 for none;
        --                               applied at every MPD start the
        --                               way mpd.consume is
        --   mpd.mixRampDb               Number or null; MPD's mixramp
        --                               threshold, which crossfades on
        --                               measured loudness rather than a
        --                               fixed overlap when the files
        --                               carry mixramp tags
        --   mpd.replayGain              off | track | album | auto
        --   ui.browseDefault            tags | folders
}

contract MpdBridge {
    status: () -> PlayerStatus
    command: (command: String) -> PlayerStatus
    capabilities: () -> Capabilities

    @invariant ReadOnlySystem
        -- Only the MPD protocol passes; the capability file is static.

    @invariant LanOnly
        -- nginx on 0.0.0.0:<ui.port>; websocat and MPD on loopback,
        -- unless mpd.exposeOnLan opens 6600 for protocol clients.

    @invariant NoRoleEnforcement
        -- The bridge does not know which page a socket came from.

    @invariant BoundedReplies
        -- No command the page sends can produce a reply larger than
        -- MPD's output buffer. Search is windowed to 200. Unfiltered
        -- tag listings are windowed. `listall` is never sent.

    @guidance
        -- websocat -t -E ws-l:127.0.0.1:8600 tcp:127.0.0.1:<mpd.port> as
        -- nixtune-websocket.service; nginx /ws proxies it; the page
        -- holds one command socket with a reply queue and one idle
        -- socket. websocat frames by TCP read, so the page accumulates a
        -- partial tail and splits on newline.
}

contract VolumeWriter {
    set: (level: Integer) -> Result

    @invariant NeverMpdSetvol
        -- On a host where volume.path is non-null, the page never sends
        -- setvol. A host with the helper configured and no connection to
        -- it reports that and writes nothing, because falling back to
        -- setvol would mute the card (decision 14).

    @invariant SameScaleAsMpd
        -- The helper writes with amixer -M, ALSA's normalized mapping,
        -- which is the scale MPD reports. The page's number and MPD's
        -- number mean the same thing.

    @invariant Glides
        -- A level change walks to its target a few units at a time
        -- rather than jumping, with the step proportional to what is
        -- left, so a tap at the far end of the bar is a fast ramp and
        -- not a step change into the speakers.

    @guidance
        -- systemd socket on 127.0.0.1:8601 with Accept=yes; the
        -- templated unit runs a shell helper with stdin and stdout on
        -- the socket; websocat bridges 8602 to it; nginx serves /volume.
        -- One line per request, "set N". The helper resolves the card
        -- index from /proc/asound/cards because alsa-lib reports a
        -- missing control device as an invalid card number.
}

contract ArtCache {
    cover: (album_path: String) -> Image?

    @invariant OneNamePerAlbum
        -- The cache writes exactly one file, cover.jpg, per album
        -- directory, so the page asks for one URL and never walks a list
        -- of names a ripper might have used.

    @invariant NeverServesAudio
        -- The nginx location matches only .jpg and .jpeg under the cache
        -- root, which contains no audio.

    @invariant Incremental
        -- An album directory whose mtime has not moved since the cache
        -- entry was written costs a stat and nothing else.

    @invariant YieldsToPlayback
        -- Nice 19, idle IO class, idle CPU policy. The first pass runs
        -- for a long while and must not be audible.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum ModuleKind {
    mpd
    | airplay
    | upnp_renderer
    | spotify_connect
    | squeezelite
    | bluetooth
    | web_ui
}

enum Role { host | guest }

enum NetworkKind { wired | wifi }

enum PlaybackState { playing | paused | stopped }

enum ScanState { never_scanned | scanning | scanned }

enum BrowseAxis { genre | artist | album | folder }

enum ReleaseStep {
    pi_plays
    | room_page
    | one_bar_and_tags
    | public_release
    | arbiter_and_renderers
    | long_tail
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

entity HardwareProfile {
    name: String
    board: String
    dac_overlay: String?
    card: String?
    mixer_control: String?
    hardware_volume: Boolean
    mpd_can_write_mixer: Boolean
    needs_pi_kernel: Boolean
}

entity HostDeclaration {
    hostname: String
    hardware: HardwareProfile
    network: NetworkKind
    ssid: String?
    psk_file: String?
    library_export: String?
    public_url: String
    host_path: String
    crossfade_seconds: Integer
    expose_mpd_on_lan: Boolean
    fleet: FleetConfig?

    modules: ModuleDeclaration with host = this
    enabled_modules: modules where enabled = true
    renderers: modules where kind in {airplay, upnp_renderer, spotify_connect, squeezelite, bluetooth}
    enabled_renderers: renderers where enabled = true

    radio_stations: RadioStation with host = this
    persisted_paths: PersistedPath with host = this
    generations: Generation with host = this
    secrets: SecretsFile? with host = this

    booted_generation: generations where status = booted
    capabilities: enabled_modules -> kind
    has_core: modules.any(m => m.kind = mpd and m.enabled)
    has_ui: modules.any(m => m.kind = web_ui and m.enabled)
    wifi_configured: ssid != null and psk_file != null
    needs_volume_helper: hardware.hardware_volume and not hardware.mpd_can_write_mixer

    invariant CoreIsMandatory {
        has_core
    }

    invariant OneBootedGeneration {
        booted_generation.count <= 1
    }

    invariant AirplayNeedsCard {
        enabled_renderers.any(r => r.kind = airplay) implies hardware.card != null
    }

    invariant HostPathIsNotRoot {
        host_path != "/"
    }

    invariant RendererDoesNotOwnTheMixer {
        -- A renderer given the mixer control writes it behind the
        -- page's back and behind the helper's. shairport-sync is
        -- configured without mixer_control_name and mixer_device, so
        -- AirPlay volume is software gain inside its own stream.
        enabled_renderers.all(r => not OwnsMixer(r))
    }

    @guidance
        -- The fleet member: hostname nixtune, deployAddr nixtune.lan,
        -- pi5-dac2hd, ssid PissiNet-5G, library export
        -- 192.168.8.110:/volume2/music/Music, AirPlay on as "nixtune",
        -- UPnP off, stations GBH 89.7 and CRB Classical 99.5,
        -- public_url http://nixtune.lan/, host_path /host,
        -- mpd.consume = true.
}

entity ModuleDeclaration {
    host: HostDeclaration
    kind: ModuleKind
    enabled: Boolean
    state: inactive | active
    is_renderer: kind in {airplay, upnp_renderer, spotify_connect, squeezelite, bluetooth}

    invariant DisabledModulesAreInactive {
        not enabled implies state = inactive
    }
}

entity SecretsFile {
    host: HostDeclaration
    path: String
    has_user_password: Boolean
    has_wifi_psk: Boolean

    @guidance
        -- Created without an editor session: values staged in
        -- $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, lengths checked, encrypted with
        -- `sops --encrypt --filename-override`, staging removed.
        -- Verification prints lengths and prefixes, never values.
}

entity OutputDevice {
    host: HostDeclaration
    profile: HardwareProfile
    owner: ModuleDeclaration?
    volume: Integer
    written_by: mpd | helper

    invariant VolumeInRange {
        volume >= 0 and volume <= 100
    }

    invariant OwnerIsEnabled {
        owner != null implies owner.enabled
    }

    invariant HelperWhereMpdCannotWrite {
        host.needs_volume_helper implies written_by = helper
    }
}

entity Player {
    host: HostDeclaration
    state: PlaybackState
    current: QueueEntry?
    queue: List<QueueEntry>
    consume: Boolean
    crossfade: Integer
    scan: ScanState
    song_count: Integer
    last_error: String?
    sessions: Session with player = this
    open_sessions: sessions where status = open
}

-- A track in the queue with who put it there.
entity QueueEntry {
    position: Integer
    track: Track
    added_by: String?
    played: Boolean
}

value PlayerStatus {
    state: PlaybackState
    current: QueueEntry?
    volume: Integer?
    queue_length: Integer
    consume: Boolean
    crossfade: Integer
    scan: ScanState
    song_count: Integer
    capabilities: Set<ModuleKind>
}

entity Session {
    player: Player
    client: Client
    role: Role
    status: open | closed
    opened_at: Timestamp
    browse: List<BrowseColumn>

    invariant GuestsAreNamed {
        role = guest implies client.nickname != null
    }
}

entity RadioStation {
    host: HostDeclaration
    name: String
    stream_url: String
    verified: Boolean
}

entity PersistedPath {
    host: HostDeclaration
    path: String
}

entity Generation {
    host: HostDeclaration
    closure: SystemClosure
    status: built | booted | previous | discarded
    built_at: Timestamp

    transitions status {
        built -> booted
        built -> discarded
        booted -> previous
        previous -> booted
        previous -> discarded
        terminal: discarded
    }
}

entity ProjectRepository {
    path: String
    public_url: String?
    main_revision: String
    nixpkgs_pin: String
    runs: UpdateRun with repo = this
    open_runs: runs where status in {opened, checked}
    issues: KnownIssue with repo = this

    invariant OneUpdateRunAtATime {
        open_runs.count <= 1
    }
}

entity UpdateRun {
    repo: ProjectRepository
    branch: String
    status: opened | checked | merged | abandoned
    ci_passed: Boolean
    lock_revision: String

    transitions status {
        opened -> checked
        opened -> abandoned
        checked -> merged
        checked -> abandoned
        terminal: merged, abandoned
    }
}

entity KnownIssue {
    repo: ProjectRepository
    name: String
    status: open | closed
    effect: String
    closes_when: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    mpd_port: Integer = 6600
    ui_port: Integer = 80
    websocket_port: Integer = 8600
    volume_socket_port: Integer = 8601
    volume_bridge_port: Integer = 8602
    max_volume: Integer = 100
    rescan_after_boot: Duration = 2.minutes
    rescan_every: Duration = 1.day
    art_scan_after_boot: Duration = 10.minutes
    art_scan_every: Duration = 6.hours
    art_long_edge: Integer = 600
    search_window: Integer = 200
    tag_window: Integer = 2000
    letter_rail_threshold: Integer = 50
    volume_glide_step: Integer = 4
    volume_glide_interval: Duration = 40.milliseconds
    default_crossfade: Integer = 0
    resume_mpd_after_renderer: Boolean = true
    current_step: ReleaseStep = one_bar_and_tags
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Defaults
------------------------------------------------------------

default HardwareProfile pi5_dac2hd = {
    name: "Raspberry Pi 5 with HiFiBerry DAC2 HD",
    board: "raspberrypi-5",
    dac_overlay: "hifiberry-dacplushd",
    card: "sndrpihifiberry",
    mixer_control: "DAC",
    hardware_volume: true,
    mpd_can_write_mixer: false,
    needs_pi_kernel: true
}

default HardwareProfile none = {
    name: "No sound card (rehearsal)",
    board: "any",
    dac_overlay: null,
    card: null,
    mixer_control: null,
    hardware_volume: false,
    mpd_can_write_mixer: true,
    needs_pi_kernel: false
}

default FleetConfig neoblade = {
    repo_path: "/home/bismuth/neoblade-config",
    input_url: "github:harryprayiv/nixtune",
    adapter_module: "modules/system/player.nix",
    build_command: "./build boot-native nixtune"
}

default ProjectRepository nixtune = {
    path: "/home/bismuth/git/nixtune",
    public_url: "https://github.com/harryprayiv/nixtune",
    main_revision: "",
    nixpkgs_pin: "6510408d147d8c5e6d76043e899e9251756f6a75"
}

default KnownIssue sd_resize = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "sd-image's online first-boot resize corrupts the root filesystem",
    status: open,
    effect: "a card that boots straight from the image as built loses directory blocks in the store; the workaround is the offline grow on winsmuth before first boot",
    closes_when: "sdImage.expandOnBoot = false in the nixtune row's extraModules (and oracle's), the offline grow written into the first-boot header of hosts/nixtune.nix, and the cause reported upstream with the e2fsck transcript"
}

default KnownIssue upmpdcli_unbuilt = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "upmpdcli hashes are lib.fakeHash",
    status: open,
    effect: "renderers.upnp cannot be enabled",
    closes_when: "nix build ~/git/nixtune#upmpdcli has been through all three hash errors; versions unverified"
}

default KnownIssue purescript_segfault = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "nixpkgs' prebuilt purs 0.15.15 segfaults on nixos-unstable newer than the pin",
    status: open,
    effect: "the public repo's lock stays on the fleet's nixpkgs revision",
    closes_when: "a newer nixpkgs builds purescript, or the page build switches to a purs built from source"
}

default KnownIssue no_impermanence = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "ext4 root without wipe-on-boot",
    status: open,
    effect: "the fleet's ext4-root warning; persistPaths mapped but inert",
    closes_when: "the rollback cycle has been rehearsed on a Pi and both Pi rows adopt it together"
}

default KnownIssue oracle_uboot = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "oracle's image would not boot if rebuilt",
    status: open,
    effect: "hosts/oracle.nix does not set hardware.raspberry-pi.firmware.uboot.enable",
    closes_when: "the option is added to hosts/oracle.nix in its own fleet commit"
}

default KnownIssue mpd_setvol_mutes_dac2hd = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "MPD's dB write path hard-mutes the HiFiBerry DAC2 HD",
    status: open,
    effect: "every setvol on this card lands on raw 0; worked around by volume.nix, which means any OTHER MPD client on the LAN, Home Assistant included, still mutes the room when it sets volume",
    closes_when: "MPD is patched or configured to take the raw write path on a control with a wide dB range, or the helper is reachable to every client, which it is not"
}

default KnownIssue listall_overruns = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "MPD closes the connection when a reply overruns its output buffer",
    status: open,
    effect: "`mpc listall` and an unwindowed `search any` both drop the client on this library; any new listing command must be windowed before it is used",
    closes_when: "max_output_buffer_size is raised in mpd.conf with a measured figure, or every listing path in the page is windowed and the rule is written into MpdBridge.BoundedReplies, which it now is"
}

default KnownIssue airplay_owns_mixer = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "shairport-sync is still given the hardware mixer",
    status: open,
    effect: "an AirPlay sender can move the room's level behind the page and behind the volume helper",
    closes_when: "mixer_control_name and mixer_device are removed from airplay.nix so AirPlay volume is software gain in its own stream"
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Boot and generations -----------------------------------------------

rule HostBootsGeneration {
    when: HostBoots(generation)
    requires: generation.status = built
    let current = host.booted_generation
    ensures:
        for g in current:
            g.status = previous
        generation.status = booted
        CoreStarted(host: host)
}

rule OperatorRollsBack {
    when: OperatorRollsBack(operator, generation)
    requires: generation.status = previous
    let current = host.booted_generation
    ensures:
        for g in current:
            g.status = previous
        generation.status = booted
}

rule CoreStartsOnBoot {
    when: CoreStarted(host)
    let core = ModuleDeclaration{host: host, kind: mpd}
    requires: exists core
    requires: core.enabled
    ensures:
        core.state = active
        output.owner = core
        player.state = stopped
        PlaybackModesApplied(player: player)
        for m in host.enabled_modules where kind != mpd:
            m.state = active

    @guidance
        -- MPD starts after network-online and the library automount,
        -- with auto_update off, so it reports ready at once regardless
        -- of library size.
}

rule PlaybackModesApplied {
    when: PlaybackModesApplied(player)
    ensures:
        if host.consume_default != null:
            player.consume = host.consume_default
        player.crossfade = host.crossfade_seconds
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- nixtune-mpd-defaults.service, a oneshot after mpd.service that
        -- retries mpc for five seconds. MPD remembers consume, random,
        -- repeat, single and crossfade in its state file across
        -- restarts, so a declared value overrides that remembered state
        -- at every start, which is what makes it a DEFAULT rather than a
        -- preference: the page's own toggle still changes it until the
        -- next start.
}

-- Library scanning ------------------------------------------------------

rule RescanTimerFires {
    when: RescanDue(host)
    requires: host.library_export != null
    requires: player.scan != scanning
    ensures:
        player.scan = scanning
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

rule DatabaseDroppedOnExportChange {
    when: CoreStarted(host)
    requires: RecordedExport(host) != host.library_export
    ensures:
        MpdDatabaseRemoved(host: host)
        RecordedExport(host) = host.library_export

    @guidance
        -- nixtune-database-stamp, a oneshot before mpd.service. MPD's
        -- URIs are relative to music_directory, so a changed export
        -- leaves a database full of URIs that resolve to nothing and a
        -- queue that fails silently. The stamp file sits beside the
        -- database and the database is deleted when they disagree.
}

rule ScanProgresses {
    when: MpdDatabaseGrew(player, count)
    requires: player.scan = scanning
    ensures:
        player.song_count = count
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

rule ScanCompletes {
    when: MpdUpdateFinished(player)
    requires: player.scan = scanning
    ensures:
        player.scan = scanned
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

-- Cover art ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule ArtScanRuns {
    when: ArtScanDue(host)
    requires: host.library_export != null
    requires: host.album_art_enabled
    ensures:
        for d in AlbumDirectories(host) where Changed(d):
            if PictureFileIn(d) != null:
                CoverWritten(album: d, from: PictureFileIn(d))
            else if EmbeddedPictureIn(FirstTrackOf(d)) != null:
                CoverWritten(album: d, from: FirstTrackOf(d))
            else:
                NoCoverMarked(album: d)

    @guidance
        -- art.nix: a oneshot with a timer, OnBootSec 10min and
        -- OnUnitActiveSec 6h, running as a fixed system user so nginx
        -- can read what it writes. A DynamicUser's state directory lives
        -- under /var/lib/private, which nginx cannot traverse, which is
        -- why the user is fixed. @eaDir and .checksums are pruned.
        -- ffmpeg takes one frame of the first video stream, which is
        -- what an attached picture is in every container it reads, and
        -- scales it down only if it is wider than art_long_edge.
        -- The unit declares RequiresMountsFor on the library, because a
        -- service runs in its own mount namespace and an automount that
        -- happens after the unit starts never appears inside it.
}

-- Sessions and roles ----------------------------------------------------

rule GuestOpensSession {
    when: ClientOpens(client, path)
    requires: client.on_lan
    requires: host.has_ui
    requires: path != host.host_path
    ensures:
        if client.nickname = null:
            client.nickname = GeneratedNickname()
        Session.created(player: player, client: client, role: guest, status: open, opened_at: now)
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

rule HostOpensSession {
    when: ClientOpens(client, path)
    requires: client.on_lan
    requires: host.has_ui
    requires: path = host.host_path
    ensures:
        Session.created(player: player, client: client, role: host, status: open, opened_at: now)
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

rule SessionCloses {
    when: ClientDisconnects(session)
    requires: session.status = open
    ensures: session.status = closed
}

-- Browsing ----------------------------------------------------------------

rule ClientBrowsesFolders {
    when: ClientBrowses(session, path)
    requires: session.status = open
    ensures: LibraryListingDelivered(session: session, path: path)

    @guidance
        -- lsinfo over the command socket, both roles.
}

rule ClientBrowsesTags {
    when: ClientSelectsTag(session, axis, value)
    requires: session.status = open
    ensures:
        for c in session.browse where c.axis is after axis:
            c.selected = null
            c.entries = TagValues(axis: c.axis, filter: SelectionsLeftOf(c))
        TagColumnsDelivered(session: session, columns: session.browse)

    @guidance
        -- `list genre`, then `list artist genre "<g>"`, then
        -- `list album artist "<a>"`, then
        -- `find album "<x>" artist "<a>"` for the tracks. Each column is
        -- bounded by the selection to its left. The exception is the
        -- leftmost column with no selection at all: `list artist` over
        -- this library is large and is windowed to tag_window, with the
        -- page saying so when it truncates.
        -- Selecting a value clears every column to its right, which is
        -- what makes the browser a path rather than a set of filters
        -- that can disagree with each other.
}

rule ClientJumpsToLetter {
    when: ClientPicksLetter(session, axis, letter)
    requires: session.status = open
    ensures: ColumnScrolledTo(session: session, axis: axis, index: FirstIndexUnder(axis, letter))

    @guidance
        -- Page-side arithmetic over a list the page already holds: no
        -- request, no backend. The rail appears on a column over
        -- letter_rail_threshold entries. A leading article is not
        -- stripped, because MPD's tag values are what they are and a
        -- page that silently reindexes them disagrees with search.
        -- Entries that do not begin with a letter land under #.
}

-- What a guest may do -----------------------------------------------------

rule GuestAppends {
    when: ClientAppends(session, uri)
    requires: session.status = open
    requires: session.role = guest
    ensures:
        MpdProtocol.apply(player, "add " + uri)
        MpdProtocol.apply(player, "sticker set song " + uri + " nixtune.added_by " + session.client.nickname)
        player.queue = player.queue + [ { position: player.queue.count, track: Track{uri: uri}, added_by: session.client.nickname } ]
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- If nothing is playing the guest page also sends `play`. That
        -- is the one transport command a guest can cause, and only from
        -- the stopped state.
}

rule GuestCommandNotOffered {
    when: ClientCommands(session, command)
    requires: session.status = open
    requires: session.role = guest
    requires: command not in {"add", "lsinfo", "list", "find", "search", "status", "currentsong", "stats", "sticker find", "idle"}
    ensures: CommandNotOffered(session: session, command: command)
}

-- What the host may do --------------------------------------------------

rule HostCommands {
    when: ClientCommands(session, command)
    requires: session.status = open
    requires: session.role = host
    ensures:
        MpdProtocol.apply(player, command)
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- Transport, random, repeat, single, consume, crossfade,
        -- clear/add/play, play <pos>, delete <pos>, move <from> <to>,
        -- seekcur <t>, load <playlist>, update. Volume is NOT here: it
        -- goes to the helper (contract VolumeWriter).
}

rule HostReordersQueue {
    when: HostDragsRow(session, from, to)
    requires: session.role = host
    requires: from != to
    ensures:
        MpdProtocol.apply(player, "move " + from + " " + to)
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- The list is never reordered under the finger. Rows are
        -- measured once, at the moment of grabbing, and each row is then
        -- DRAWN offset from where it sits, so the geometry the drag is
        -- reckoned against stays still while the gap appears to open.
        -- One move goes out when the pointer lifts and the real order
        -- comes back through the idle connection like any other change.
        -- Pointer events on the handle and arrow keys when the handle
        -- has focus reach the same command, so there is no mouse-only
        -- path. No FFI: Halogen's own event handling covers all of it.
}

rule HostSeesAttribution {
    when: PlayerStatusChanged(player)
    for s in player.open_sessions where role = host:
        ensures: QueueDelivered(session: s, queue: player.queue)

    @guidance
        -- ONE command: `sticker find song "" nixtune.added_by` returns
        -- every attribution in the database, and the page subscribes to
        -- the `sticker` idle subsystem to stay current. The per-entry
        -- form this replaced cost one round trip per queue entry on
        -- every queue change and never recorded a miss. See decision 17.
}

rule HostShowsQr {
    when: HostOpensQr(session)
    requires: session.role = host
    ensures: QrDelivered(session: session, url: host.public_url)
}

-- Volume -----------------------------------------------------------------

rule ClientSetsVolume {
    when: HostSetsVolume(session, level)
    requires: session.role = host
    requires: level >= 0 and level <= host.max_volume
    ensures:
        if host.needs_volume_helper:
            VolumeWriter.set(level)
        else:
            MpdProtocol.apply(player, "setvol " + level)
        -- The level the page SHOWS always comes back from MPD's mixer
        -- idle event, whoever moved it.
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

rule ProtocolClientSetsVolume {
    when: ProtocolClientCommands(protocol_client, "setvol", level)
    requires: host.expose_mpd_on_lan
    ensures:
        MpdProtocol.apply(player, "setvol " + level)
        if host.needs_volume_helper:
            OutputMuted(output: output)

    @guidance
        -- Stated as a rule because it is a real consequence and not a
        -- hypothetical: Home Assistant's media_player.volume_set sends
        -- setvol, and on this card that silences the room. Use HA for
        -- transport until KnownIssue mpd_setvol_mutes_dac2hd closes.
}

-- Status fan-out --------------------------------------------------------

rule StatusPushedToSessions {
    when: PlayerStatusChanged(player)
    for s in player.open_sessions:
        ensures: StatusDelivered(session: s, status: {
            state: player.state,
            current: player.current,
            volume: output.volume,
            queue_length: player.queue.count,
            consume: player.consume,
            crossfade: player.crossfade,
            scan: player.scan,
            song_count: player.song_count,
            capabilities: host.capabilities
        })
}

-- Output arbitration ------------------------------------------------------

rule RendererAcquiresOutput {
    when: RendererStreamStarts(module)
    requires: module.enabled
    requires: module.is_renderer
    requires: module.state = active
    requires: output.owner = null or output.owner.kind = mpd
    ensures:
        if player.state = playing:
            player.state = paused
        output.owner = module
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

rule RendererReleasesOutput {
    when: RendererStreamStops(module)
    requires: output.owner = module
    let core = ModuleDeclaration{host: host, kind: mpd}
    ensures:
        output.owner = core
        if config.resume_mpd_after_renderer and player.state = paused:
            player.state = playing
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

-- Project maintenance ---------------------------------------------------

rule MaintainerOpensUpdateRun {
    when: MaintainerRunsFlakeUpdate(maintainer)
    requires: module_repo.open_runs.count = 0
    ensures:
        UpdateRun.created(repo: module_repo, branch: "update", status: opened, ci_passed: false, lock_revision: "")
}

rule CiChecksUpdateRun {
    when: CiCompletes(run, passed)
    requires: run.status = opened
    ensures:
        run.status = checked
        run.ci_passed = passed
}

rule MaintainerMergesUpdateRun {
    when: MaintainerMerges(maintainer, run)
    requires: run.status = checked
    requires: run.ci_passed
    ensures:
        run.status = merged
        module_repo.main_revision = run.lock_revision
        FleetInputBumped(fleet: fleet_repo, revision: run.lock_revision)
}

rule MaintainerClosesIssue {
    when: IssueFixed(issue, revision)
    requires: issue.status = open
    ensures: issue.status = closed
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant SingleOutputOwner {
    for d in OutputDevices:
        d.owner != null implies d.owner.state = active
}

invariant GuestsNeverRemove {
    -- Over the page's own surface. Not over the websocket (decision 8).
    for s in Sessions where role = guest:
        s.status = open implies not Offered(s, "delete") and not Offered(s, "clear") and not Offered(s, "move")
}

invariant NicknamesAreBrowserState {
    for c in Clients:
        c.nickname != null implies StoredIn(c.nickname, "localStorage")
}

invariant ScanNeverBlocksStart {
    for p in Players:
        p.scan = scanning implies ModuleDeclaration{host: p.host, kind: mpd}.state = active
}

invariant TransportIsAlwaysReachable {
    -- Decision 18. Browsing a library the size of this one takes minutes,
    -- and a track that needs skipping does not wait for the browse to
    -- finish.
    for s in Sessions where role = host:
        s.status = open implies Offered(s, "transport") and Offered(s, "volume")
}

invariant NoUnboundedListing {
    -- KnownIssue listall_overruns.
    for c in CommandsThePageSends:
        Unbounded(c) implies Windowed(c)
}

invariant PageNeverSetvolsAHelperHost {
    for h in HostDeclarations where needs_volume_helper:
        not PageSends(h, "setvol")
}

invariant MainIsAlwaysChecked {
    for r in UpdateRuns:
        r.status = merged implies r.ci_passed
}

invariant UpnpOffWhileUnbuilt {
    for h in HostDeclarations:
        upmpdcli_unbuilt.status = open implies not h.enabled_renderers.any(r => r.kind = upnp_renderer)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

actor Guest {
    identified_by: Session where role = guest
}

actor Host {
    identified_by: Session where role = host
}

actor Operator {
    identified_by: Client where on_lan = true
}

actor Maintainer {
    identified_by: Client where on_lan = true
}

actor Automation {
    identified_by: ProtocolClient where kind = home_assistant
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface GuestPage {
    facing guest: Guest

    exposes:
        player.state
        player.current
        player.current.added_by
        player.current.track.format
        player.scan
        player.song_count
        host.hostname
        guest.client.nickname

    provides:
        ClientBrowses(session, path)
        ClientSelectsTag(session, axis, value)
        ClientPicksLetter(session, axis, letter)
        ClientAppends(session, uri)
        ClientDisconnects(session)

    contracts:
        demands MpdBridge

    @guarantee AppendOnlyByConstruction
        -- No control that sends a queue command other than add (and play
        -- from the stopped state).

    @guarantee NoVolumeNoQueue
        -- No volume, no queue view, no transport.

    @guidance
        -- Two views: Now playing (cover, title, artist/album, the format
        -- badge, progress, "added by", the scan indicator in the header,
        -- "you are <nickname>" in the footer) and Library (the tag
        -- browser with the folder tree as a fourth axis, a search box, a
        -- + on each entry). Phone-first, dark by default.
}

surface HostPage {
    facing host: Host

    exposes:
        player.state
        player.current
        player.queue
        player.consume
        player.crossfade
        player.scan
        player.song_count
        player.last_error
        output.volume
        host.public_url
        for m in host.enabled_modules:
            m.kind
        for s in host.radio_stations:
            s.name

    provides:
        ClientCommands(session, command)
        HostSetsVolume(session, level)
        HostDragsRow(session, from, to)
        ClientBrowses(session, path)
        ClientSelectsTag(session, axis, value)
        ClientPicksLetter(session, axis, letter)
        HostOpensQr(session)
        ClientDisconnects(session)

    contracts:
        demands MpdBridge
        demands VolumeWriter
        demands ArtCache

    @guarantee NoSettingsSurface
        -- Hardware, modules, sources and stations are shown, never
        -- edited. Playback modes are not settings: consume, random,
        -- repeat, single and crossfade are MPD state and the page
        -- changes them.

    @guidance
        -- Views: Now playing, Queue, Library, Radio, QR. Below all of
        -- them, on every view, ONE transport bar: previous,
        -- play/pause, next, mute, the level slider, and at 30rem and up
        -- the typed level field and the steppers. Decision 18.
        -- Now playing keeps the cover, the format badges and the seek
        -- bar; it loses the transport row, which moved into the bar.
        -- Queue rows carry a drag handle, the format badge, the
        -- attribution and a remove button; rows the player has passed
        -- are dimmed and struck through unless random is on, in which
        -- case the order is not the order they were heard in and nothing
        -- is dimmed.
}

surface Automation {
    facing automation: Automation

    exposes:
        player.state
        player.current
        player.queue
        output.volume

    provides:
        ProtocolClientCommands(protocol_client, command, argument)

    contracts:
        demands MpdBridge

    @guarantee NothingIsAdded
        -- Home Assistant speaks the MPD protocol on port 6600. The
        -- module contributes one boolean, mpd.exposeOnLan, and a
        -- firewall port. There is no nixtune-specific integration, no
        -- API and no second protocol.

    @guarantee SameTrustAsTheRoom
        -- An unauthenticated client on the LAN with full MPD rights,
        -- which is decision 8's trust model applied to a different kind
        -- of client.

    @guidance
        -- Transport, queue and playlist control work. Volume does not:
        -- see KnownIssue mpd_setvol_mutes_dac2hd and rule
        -- ProtocolClientSetsVolume.
}

surface FleetDeployment {
    facing operator: Operator

    exposes:
        host.hostname
        host.network
        for g in host.generations:
            g.status
        for i in module_repo.issues where status = open:
            i.name
            i.effect

    provides:
        OperatorRollsBack(operator, generation) when host.generations.any(g => g.status = previous)

    contracts:
        demands PlayerModule

    @guarantee FleetShape
        -- One row, one adapter, two host files; deployAddr is a name.

    @guidance
        -- Day to day: edit ~/git/nixtune, commit, PUSH, then in the
        -- fleet `nix flake update nixtune --tarball-ttl 0`,
        -- `./build check`, `./build deploy-native nixtune`, live with
        -- it, `./build boot-native nixtune`. The push is not optional:
        -- the input is a GitHub input and an unpushed change is
        -- invisible to the fleet.
}

surface CommunityFlake {
    facing adopter: Operator

    exposes:
        module_repo.public_url
        module_repo.nixpkgs_pin
        for i in module_repo.issues where status = open:
            i.name

    contracts:
        demands PlayerModule

    @guarantee StandaloneUse
        -- Import nixosModules.default, set services.nixtune.*, import
        -- nixos-hardware's raspberry-pi-5 for the Pi profile.

    @guidance
        -- AGPLv3 (LICENSE still to be added). No moOde code or name.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Out of Scope: the DJ console
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Recorded here rather than as a release step, because it is a
-- different product and pretending otherwise would let it erode this
-- one by increments. Decision 22.
--
--   What it needs that MPD cannot give:
--     - two decks sounding at once, each with its own transport
--     - independent tempo and pitch, with time-stretch, per deck
--     - cue points, and a preview path that is not the room's output
--     - a crossfader, and per-deck gain and EQ
--     - beat and tempo detection, offline, cached per track
--   What that implies:
--     - an audio engine on the Pi, which is an application server, which
--       contradicts decision 3
--     - state that outlives a generation (cue points, analysis, crates),
--       which contradicts decision 1 unless it is declared data rather
--       than configuration
--     - a second ALSA client, or one engine that owns the card and MPD
--       feeding it, which changes the arbitration story completely
--
--   What it would SHARE with nixtune: the library and its mount, the
--   hardware profile, the volume helper, the art cache, the fleet row,
--   and the page's design language. That sharing is the argument for
--   building it beside nixtune rather than inside it.
--
--   What is in scope for nixtune and covers most of a party anyway:
--   crossfade (mpd.crossfade and mixramp), consume as the default queue
--   discipline, replay gain so one record is not twice the volume of the
--   next, a queue that is pleasant to reorder under load, and the tag
--   browser and letter rail that make finding the next record fast.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred MpdProtocol.apply          -- see: https://mpd.readthedocs.io/en/latest/protocol.html
deferred MpdProtocol.stickers       -- see: the sticker commands in the same document
deferred MpdProtocol.tagListing     -- see: the `list` and `find` commands in the same document
deferred MpdProtocol.crossfade      -- see: crossfade, mixrampdb, mixrampdelay
deferred Firmware.configtxt         -- see: nixos-hardware raspberry-pi/README.md
deferred Renderer.airplay           -- see: shairport-sync documentation
deferred Renderer.upnp_renderer     -- see: upmpdcli documentation
deferred Websocket.bridge           -- see: websocat documentation
deferred AlsaMixer.mapped           -- see: amixer -M and ALSA's normalized volume mapping
deferred Automation.homeassistant   -- see: Home Assistant's MPD integration
deferred Fleet.rows                 -- see: neoblade-config.allium

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Whether page-side role limits (decision 8) stay acceptable once the player is used by people outside the household; the upgrade is a filtering proxy between websocat and MPD, which is the backend the decision avoided."
open question "How a protocol client such as Home Assistant should set volume on a card MPD cannot write. A filtering proxy on 6600 that rewrites setvol into a call to the helper would fix it and would also give decision 8 its enforcement point, which suggests both problems have one answer."
open question "Whether DSP should be a declared option with a rebuild to change it, or a declared option plus a coefficient file in a persisted path that something on the Pi can write. The second is better to use and is the first crack in decision 1."
open question "Whether the DJ console is built beside nixtune sharing its library and hardware layer, or whether nixtune's page grows a second mode and the no-backend decision is dropped. The spec assumes the first; nothing has been built either way."
open question "Whether the tag browser's leftmost column should be genre at all. Genre tags in a library this size are inconsistent enough that artist-first with genre as a filter chip may be the better shape. This is answerable by looking at `list genre` on the real database and counting."
open question "Whether the letter rail should strip leading articles. Not stripping disagrees with nobody; stripping disagrees with MPD's own sort order and with search."
open question "Whether a guest's `play` from the stopped state is welcome at 2 a.m."
open question "Whether the same file added by two guests should show both names; stickers hold one value per URI."
open question "Why nixpkgs' online expandOnBoot resize corrupted directory blocks on this card and kernel, and whether it reproduces on a second card."
